            <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="mg-maths">
                <div class="section-heading">
                    <p class="eyebrow">03 — How the pages are built</p>
                    <h2 id="mg-maths">Polar coordinates, rotations and closed regions.</h2>
                    <p>
                        Geometry, composition and SVG rendering are separate,
                        small modules. Geometry is plain numbers and tuples,
                        which is why it ports to JavaScript so directly.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="version-row">
                    {versions.map((v) => (
                        <article class="card">
                            <span class="version-badge">v{v.version}</span>
                            <h3>{v.name}</h3>
                            <p>{v.text}</p>
                        </article>
                    ))}
                </div>

                <div class="maths-grid">
                    <article class="card code-card">
                        <h3>One closed petal</h3>
                        <p>From <code>src/rocketeers/geometry.py</code>. Both sides meet where <code>sin(πt) = 0</code>, so every petal is a closed region.</p>
                        <pre class="code"><code>{codeExcerpt}</code></pre>
                    </article>

                    <article class="card">
                        <h3>Construction rules (v3)</h3>
                        <ul class="dot-list">
                            <li><strong>Rotation:</strong> each sector is repeated by θ = 2πj/N; reflection maps (x, y) to (x, −y) and flips an arc's sweep flag.</li>
                            <li><strong>Vesica lenses:</strong> for axial endpoints a distance d apart, R = d/√3, so two equal circles meet exactly at the endpoints.</li>
                            <li><strong>Star polygons:</strong> the valley radius of a skip-m star is r = R·cos(mπ/N) / cos((m−1)π/N); only outer chord portions are drawn.</li>
                            <li><strong>Considered and rejected:</strong> rose curves, because repeated returns to the origin crowd the centre.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p class="small">Summarised from <code>docs/mathematical-construction.md</code>.</p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="mg-export">
